93fc1a3d9320f85606e1a0", "format": "Metadata"}, {"name": "THEBATWHISPERSspecial65mmWidescreenEdition_meta.xml", "source": "original", "mtime": "1591612648", "size": "5825", "format": "Metadata", "md5": "d69963d6587a93a960a81045908d8173", "crc32": "bd2a0ffd", "sha1": "ad6b06b02771661e47fad0aea267dfbfb50e78b2"}, {"name": "THEBATWHISPERSspecial65mmWidescreenEdition_reviews.xml", "source": "original", "mtime": "1781962175", "size": "4919", "md5": "79ddea983eb4498f98bb5380dc47bfa9", "crc32": "e4bdb3e3", "sha1": "eca7c11e11cdea46a81bb5c36fe1e87be339c739", "format": "Metadata"}, {"name": "__ia_thumb.jpg", "source": "original", "mtime": "1616275249", "size": "2621", "md5": "cfa01fd36d75b864075dde1a76b3f097", "crc32": "bf99419f", "sha1": "d1b75e59c0530286b247d7c4a8753bf30df3bccc", "format": "Item Tile", "rotation": "0"}], "files_count": 94, "item_last_updated": 1781962177, "item_size": 1222755777, "metadata": {"identifier": "THEBATWHISPERSspecial65mmWidescreenEdition", "mediatype": "movies", "collection": ["feature_films_picfixer", "feature_films", "moviesandfilms"], "description": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\">SPECIAL NOTE: This film was shot in two versions with a different director of photography for each. One is in standard 35mm and the other in an early 65mm widescreen process. The Depression and then WW2 stalled further widescreen development until the the late \u201840s.</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">\u201cMasterful cinema\u201d \u201cTotally grand fun!\u201d \u201cSurprisingly scary\u201d \u201cGreat atmosphere and impressive sets\u201d \u201cSilly, hokey and Wonderful\u201d (IMDB reviews quotes).\u00a0\u00a0</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">Murder mystery, suspense and comedy based on a successful stage play by Mary Roberts Rinehart and Avery Hopwood. Good cast and good production noted for its innovative visuals, Eighty minutes plus of old-dark-house fun. Remade in 1937 as \u201cSh! The Octopus,\u201d in 1939 as \u201cThe Gorilla\u201d and in 1956 as \u201cThe Bat.\u201d IMDB rating 6.5.</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">Directed by Roland West.</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">Released in 1930.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">Complete Print</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">AKA \u201cRoland West\u2019s The Bat Whispers\u201d</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial;font-size:14pt;\">TRIVIA: Allegedly this film was Bob Kane\u2019s inspiration for Batman.</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"><br /></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"><br /></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:3.7pt;margin-bottom:3.7pt;border-width:1pt;border-style:solid;padding:10pt 10pt 12pt;background:rgb(255,255,255);\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:14pt;\"><br /></span></p><p></p>", "licenseurl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/", "scanner": "Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.4", "subject": "Mysteries; murder mysteries; whodunits; old dark house; Crayce Hampton; Maude Eburne; Una Merkel; Chester Morris; Spencer Charters; Gustav von Seyffertitz", "title": "THE BAT WHISPERS (special 65mm widescreen edition)", "publicdate": "2019-05-12 17:04:30", "uploader": "bobmeyer104@earthlink.net", "addeddate": "2019-05-12 17:04:30", "creator": "Joseph M Schenck", "publisher": "Art Cinema Corporation", "sound": "sound", "color": "B&W", "backup_location": "ia906903_32"}, "reviews": [{"reviewtitle": "Well, Alrighty Then!", "reviewbody": "65mm widescreen edition?  1930?\nI CALL \"BULLSHIT\"!\nThere was NO SUCH THING in 1930!  Widescreen NEVER EXISTED THEN!\nThis movie was cropped & stretched to fit the widescreen format!\nWhy people try presenting something as what it's not is BULLSHIT!\nYou cropped & stretched the video to misrepresent the true aspect ratio!  Which makes you A FREAKING LIAR AND A JACKASS!", "stars": "0", "reviewer": "sammyk1964", "reviewdate": "2021-03-20 21:19:25", "createdate": "2021-03-20 21:19:25", "reviewer_itemname": "@sammyk1964"}, {"reviewtitle": "Yes, there was such a thing as 65mm....", "reviewbody": "sammyk1964 - maybe do a five second google search:\n\nhttp://www.widescreenmuseum.com/special/65mm_bat.htm\n\nhttps://www.in70mm.com/news/2005/bat_whispers/index.htm\n\n\n\n ", "stars": "0", "reviewer": "SighingFlosser", "reviewdate": "2025-08-15 02:53:12", "createdate": "2021-04-10 06:44:20", "reviewer_itemname": "@sighingflosser"}, {"reviewtitle": "Coming to the defense of the original uploader.", "reviewbody": "I myself own the rare out of print 1999 DVD edition of this 1930 movie. There are indeed 2 versions. One is the standard 35mm edition. The other is a unique 65mm wide-screen edition. This was the only film done in the experimental 65mm process. The clown giving you a hard time doesn't know what you are talking about. You didn't crop or stretch anything. The 1999 DVD has both versions. I felt the need to come on the record and set the record straight. This technology did exist in 1930. It just wasn't widely used. That's all. And that clown is too lazy to do his own research. Boy does that guy look stupid. Thanks for the upload. Just completed the download of the 65mm. I will present it on my YouTube channel at some point in time. ", "stars": "5", "reviewer": "Robert Michael Jensen", "reviewdate": "2023-04-18 05:58:19", "createdate": "2023-04-18 05:58:19", "reviewer_itemname": "@robert_michael_jensen"}, {"reviewtitle": "\ud83d\udc4d Love this movie", "reviewbody": "Idiot crying about no 65mm. Enjoy the movie, be thankful we can see this iconic film. It is what it is ! Leave the arguments on Capitol Hill where the true idiots ruin our country. Very clear copy, excellent audio.", "stars": "5", "reviewer": "1969nam", "reviewdate": "2024-02-12 23:37:02", "createdate": "2024-02-12 23:37:02", "reviewer_itemname": "@1969nam"}, {"reviewtitle": "I wish people would check facts before befor moaning to uploader", "reviewbody": "I checked on IMDB under cast and Crew for Cameramen and found that it was indeed filmed twice as a new test for 65mm widescreen.\nCinematography by \nRay June\t...\t(35mm version)\nRobert H. Planck\t...\t(70mm version)\n\nAlso this was on the main page under \"Did You Know\"\nAlternate versions\nThis film was shot in two versions with a different director of photography for each. One is in standard 35mm and the other in an early 65mm process. The 65mm version is considered \"stagebound\" (it was actually based on a popular play) while the 35mm version is considered more \"cinematic\". Prints of both versions still exist.", "stars": "4", "reviewer": "3D Phil", "reviewdate": "2024-03-04 18:42:07", "createdate": "2024-03-04 18:42:07", "reviewer_itemname": "@3d_phil"}, {"reviewtitle": "Question", "reviewbody": "I know it say's it's public domain, but I posted this movie on my youtube and got a removal request the next day.. someone must own the rights to it now? Just letting yall know.", "stars": "0", "reviewer": "wendylynne1", "reviewdate": "2024-04-23 23:37:31", "createdate": "2024-04-23 23:37:31", "reviewer_itemname": "@wendylynne1"}, {"reviewtitle": "RE Batman", "reviewbody": "Kane was inspired by certain shots of the film (the hand close up etc), but let's be honest.... Batman is made up of the Shadow and Green Hornet.", "stars": "0", "reviewer": "NKTRGZT", "reviewdate": "2026-05-07 15:08:36", "createdate": "2026-05-07 15:08:36", "reviewer_itemname": "@nktrgzt"}], "server": "dn801206.us.archive.org", "simplelists": {"solo_manifest": {"solo_manifest_dn801206": {"sys_changed_by": {"source": "task", "task_id": "5453914920"}, "sys_last_changed": "2026-06-20 13:29:46.859211"}}}, "solo": true, "uniq": 1978386915, "workable_servers": ["dn801206.us.archive.org"]}